{# A LISTING WITHOUT COLUMNS — `table`'s twin below the header, and the same cell.

   IT IMPORTS THE MACRO RATHER THAN OWNING ONE. `cell()` is declared by
   `table.twig` and imported here by component id, so a badge in a table cell and
   a badge in a list item are ONE code path and not two that agree. The address is
   a component id and not a file path because that is the only form that resolves
   in both environments: Drupal's component loader resolves component ids only,
   and the `@bb_theme` namespace points at different directories in Drupal and
   in Storybook — so `@bb_theme/_cell.twig` would name two different files.
   Importing a template runs none of its body; this costs the macro and nothing
   else.

   NO `<tr>` AND NO `<td>`, and that is asserted rather than intended. A listing
   without columns that drew table markup would be a table pretending not to be
   one, which is what a flex grid with fixed widths always turns out to be.

   A REAL `<ul>` OF `<li>`, which is the accessibility half of this change. The
   three entry components this absorbed had to declare `role="listitem"` on
   themselves and depend on a generic container being told to announce
   `role="list"` — an arrangement that breaks the moment either half is composed
   somewhere else, because the two roles must be direct parent and child or a
   browser drops both. A real list needs none of it. The explicit `role="list"`
   below is not that workaround returning: Tailwind's reset removes the list style,
   and a `<ul>` with no marker loses its list semantics in some browsers, so the
   role restores what the reset took.

   THE TWO DENSITIES ARE ONE PROP. `lines` is the dense form — one line per item,
   a hairline between them, no surface — and `cards` gives each item the surface,
   border and radius the theme already uses for a thing read one at a time. The
   items and the cells are identical in both, which is exactly why this is `layout`
   and not a second component.

   `pattern` IS THE LISTING ROW. With it, an item is one GitLab-style row — a
   headline line and a meta line on the left, one compact column on the right —
   and the prop names which cell keys fill which region, so the four operator
   listings share this one implementation and differ only in their props. An
   optional leading `avatar` and a `description` line beneath the meta line
   make a project or group row recognisable at a glance.
   Without it, the cell flow below is exactly what it was. #}
{% import 'bb_theme:table' as cells %}

{% set cards = layout == 'cards' %}
{#- `spacing: comfortable` reaches cards only: one spacing step more between and
    inside the cards, for a roster read person by person. #}
{% set roomy = cards and spacing == 'comfortable' %}
{#- THE LEADING STATUS RAIL, drawn with a pseudo-element so it costs no cell. On a
    card it runs the full height and picks up the left radius, exactly as the
    board's card does; on a line it is inset top and bottom, exactly as the run
    line was. `wait` and `critical` additionally tint the whole item — the states
    that need a person — and on a card the tint covers the border too, because a
    card has one to tint. #}
{% set accent_map = {
  'running': 'bg-state-running',
  'attention': 'bg-state-attention-mark',
  'wait': 'bg-state-unassigned',
  'critical': 'bg-state-unassigned',
  'idle': 'bg-transparent'
} %}
{#- The detail line takes the ink of its item's accent, so a failure reads red
    and a waiting claim amber; any other item keeps the light text colour. #}
{% set detail_map = {
  'wait': 'text-state-unassigned-ink',
  'critical': 'text-state-unassigned-ink',
  'attention': 'text-state-attention-ink'
} %}
{% set rail_classes = cards
  ? ['absolute', 'left-0', 'top-0', 'bottom-0', 'w-1', 'rounded-l-xs']
  : ['absolute', 'left-0', 'top-2', 'bottom-2', 'w-1', 'rounded-xs'] %}
{#- `plain` is a block's property rows: no line, hover fill or inset. The
    label cell takes a fixed `w-28` track so values align; values may wrap
    anywhere, since clipping would also clip an inline picker's panel. #}
{% set plain = layout == 'plain' %}
{% set item_base = plain
  ? ['group', 'relative', 'flex', 'items-center', 'flex-wrap', 'gap-x-inline', 'gap-y-inline-xs', 'py-inline-xs']
  : (cards
  ? ['group', 'relative', 'flex', 'items-center', 'flex-wrap', 'gap-x-stack', 'gap-y-inline-xs', 'min-h-row', 'pl-stack', 'pr-inline', roomy ? 'py-stack' : 'py-inline', 'bg-surface-2', 'border', 'border-border-2', 'rounded-xs', 'transition-colors', 'duration-fast', 'hover:bg-surface-3']
  : ['group', 'relative', 'flex', 'items-center', 'flex-wrap', 'gap-stack', 'pl-stack', 'pr-inline', 'py-inline', 'border-b', 'border-border-2', 'last:border-b-0', 'transition-colors', 'duration-fast', 'hover:bg-surface']) %}
{% if items is not empty %}
  <ul{{ (attributes ?: create_attribute()).addClass(['flex', 'flex-col', 'list-none', 'p-0', 'm-0', cards ? (roomy ? 'gap-stack' : 'gap-inline') : 'gap-0']) }} role="list">
    {% for item in items %}
      {% set item_classes = item_base %}
      {% if item.accent in ['wait', 'critical'] %}
        {% set item_classes = item_classes|merge(['bg-state-unassigned-tint']) %}
      {% endif %}
      {#- A detail line sits close under its cells: the line gap shrinks, the
          gap between cells stays. -#}
      {% if item.detail and not cards and not plain and not pattern %}
        {% set item_classes = item_classes|filter(c => c != 'gap-stack')|merge(['gap-x-stack', 'gap-y-inline-xs']) %}
      {% endif %}
      {#- THE WHOLE PATTERNED ROW IS A CLICK TARGET FOR ITS IDENTITY LINK. A click on
          the row's own surface forwards to the first link in the headline, so htmx
          boost, the second click and the keyboard stay the real link's; a click on
          any control or link inside the row, or one that ends a text selection, is
          left alone. No overlay anchor and no new tab stop. Only a row whose
          headline carries a link opts in, and the cursor says so. -#}
      {%- set row_link = false -%}
      {%- if pattern -%}
        {%- for key in pattern.headline|default([]) -%}
          {%- set c = item.cells[key]|default(null) -%}
          {%- if c and (c.kind|default('') == 'link' or (c.kind|default('') == 'rendered' and '<a' in (c.markup ~ ''))) -%}{%- set row_link = true -%}{%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      {%- endif -%}
      {#- The regions a patterned row fills, read before the item opens: a row
          with a meta or description line under its headline is a two-line row. -#}
      {% set left = [] %}
      {% if pattern %}
        {% set captions = pattern.captions|default({}) %}
        {% set right = [] %}
        {% set right_meta = [] %}
        {% set avatar = [] %}
        {% for region in ['avatar', 'headline', 'meta', 'description', 'right', 'right_meta'] %}
          {% set present = [] %}
          {% for key in pattern[region]|default([]) %}
            {% if item.cells[key]|default(null) %}{% set present = present|merge([key]) %}{% endif %}
          {% endfor %}
          {% if region == 'right' %}
            {% set right = present %}
          {% elseif region == 'right_meta' %}
            {% set right_meta = present %}
          {% elseif region == 'avatar' %}
            {% set avatar = present %}
          {% elseif present is not empty %}
            {% set left = left|merge([{ 'region': region, 'keys': present }]) %}
          {% endif %}
        {% endfor %}
      {% endif %}
      {#- A TWO-LINE ROW IN `lines` IS 56PX for a one-line title (`min-h-14`): the
          lines sit without a gap and the inset shrinks to `inline-xs`, so a meta
          line with an avatar or badge still fits; a wrapping title grows the row. -#}
      {% set two_line = pattern and not cards and not plain and left|length > 1 %}
      {% if two_line %}
        {% set item_classes = item_classes|filter(c => c != 'py-inline')|merge(['py-inline-xs', 'min-h-14']) %}
      {% endif %}
      {%- if row_link %}{% set item_classes = item_classes|merge(['cursor-pointer']) %}{% endif %}
      <li data-list-item class="{{ item_classes|join(' ') }}"{% if item.url %} data-item-url="{{ item.url }}"{% endif %}{% if row_link %} x-data @click="$event.target.closest('a, button, input, select, textarea, label, summary, [role=button]') || String(window.getSelection()) || $el.querySelector('[data-list-region=headline] a')?.click()"{% endif %}>
        <span class="{{ (rail_classes|merge([accent_map[item.accent]|default('bg-transparent')]))|join(' ') }}" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        {%- if pattern %}
          {#- THE PATTERNED ROW (BB-592): a headline line (one type step up, `text-item-title`) and a meta line in a
              flexible left block, one compact right block that never exceeds the row. Each region walks its
              own key list in order and skips absent cells, so an optional fact
              leaves no gap. The left block's basis is what makes the right block
              flow beneath it on a narrow viewport and sit at the right edge on a
              wide one; `min-w-0` keeps a long unbroken identity
              inside the row instead of widening the document. `wrap-anywhere` lets an
              unbroken word wrap and `*:min-w-0` lets a cell's own element (a plain
              owner link, say) shrink as a flex item; `person` keeps its truncation. #}
          {#- `avatar` leads the row as its own non-shrinking block, before the text
              column; `description` is the text column's last line, beneath meta,
              and wraps inside the row. Both are optional regions like the rest. #}
          {#- With an avatar, avatar and text share one non-wrapping block that takes
              the left basis, so the avatar stays beside the headline on a phone
              and only the right block flows beneath. A headline alone centres on the
              avatar; once a meta or description line follows, both align at the top. -#}
          {% if avatar is not empty %}
            <div class="flex min-w-0 flex-1 basis-80 {{ left|length > 1 ? 'items-start' : 'items-center' }} gap-stack">
            <div data-list-region="avatar" class="flex shrink-0 items-center gap-inline-xs">
              {% for key in avatar %}
                <span class="flex shrink-0" data-cell="{{ key }}">{{ cells.cell(item.cells[key]) }}</span>
              {% endfor %}
            </div>
          {% endif %}
          {% if left is not empty %}
            <div class="flex min-w-0 flex-1 {{ avatar is empty ? 'basis-80' : 'basis-0' }} flex-col {{ two_line ? 'gap-0' : 'gap-inline-xs' }}">
              {% for line in left %}
                <div data-list-region="{{ line.region }}" class="{{ (line.region == 'headline' ? ['flex', 'min-w-0', 'flex-wrap', 'items-center', 'gap-x-inline', 'gap-y-inline-xs', 'text-item-title', 'text-text'] : (line.region == 'description' ? ['flex', 'min-w-0', 'flex-wrap', 'gap-x-stack', 'gap-y-inline-xs', 'text-body', 'text-text-light'] : ['flex', 'min-w-0', 'flex-wrap', 'items-center', 'gap-x-stack', 'gap-y-inline-xs', 'text-meta', 'text-text-faint']))|join(' ') }}">
                  {% for key in line.keys %}
                    <span class="min-w-0 wrap-anywhere *:min-w-0" data-cell="{{ key }}">{% if captions[key]|default('') %}<span data-cell-label class="mr-inline-xs text-meta text-text-faint">{{ captions[key] }}</span>{% endif %}{{ cells.cell(item.cells[key]) }}</span>
                  {% endfor %}
                </div>
              {% endfor %}
            </div>
          {% endif %}
          {% if avatar is not empty %}</div>{% endif %}
          {#- THE RIGHT BLOCK IS A SMALL COLUMN: the `right` cells on top and the
              `right_meta` line beneath them, right-aligned and faint like a caption.
              It still flows beneath the left block on a narrow viewport. -#}
          {% if right is not empty or right_meta is not empty %}
            <div class="ml-auto flex min-w-0 max-w-full flex-col items-end gap-inline-xs">
              {% if right is not empty %}
                <div data-list-region="right" class="flex min-w-0 max-w-full flex-wrap items-center justify-end gap-inline">
                  {% for key in right %}
                    <span class="flex min-w-0 max-w-full items-center wrap-anywhere *:min-w-0" data-cell="{{ key }}">{% if captions[key]|default('') %}<span data-cell-label class="mr-inline-xs text-meta text-text-faint">{{ captions[key] }}</span>{% endif %}{{ cells.cell(item.cells[key]) }}</span>
                  {% endfor %}
                </div>
              {% endif %}
              {% if right_meta is not empty %}
                <div data-list-region="right_meta" class="flex min-w-0 max-w-full flex-wrap items-center justify-end gap-x-stack gap-y-inline-xs text-meta text-text-faint">
                  {% for key in right_meta %}
                    <span class="flex min-w-0 max-w-full items-center wrap-anywhere *:min-w-0" data-cell="{{ key }}">{% if captions[key]|default('') %}<span data-cell-label class="mr-inline-xs text-meta text-text-faint">{{ captions[key] }}</span>{% endif %}{{ cells.cell(item.cells[key]) }}</span>
                  {% endfor %}
                </div>
              {% endif %}
            </div>
          {% endif %}
        {%- else %}
        {#- ONE CELL PER ENTRY OF THE MAP, in the order the mapping wrote them.
            There are no columns here, so the key names the value instead of
            addressing a column, and the item's own order is the only order there
            is — which is the difference this component exists to state.
            In `lines` the `action` cells form one group at the right edge, in
            their own order: the group wraps as a whole when the line is full,
            so no action is left behind at the start of the next line. #}
        {% set actions = not cards and not plain ? item.cells|filter(c => c and c.kind|default('') == 'action') : {} %}
        {% for key, c in item.cells %}
          {% if c and actions[key] is not defined %}<span class="min-w-0 {{ not plain ? 'whitespace-nowrap' : (loop.first ? 'whitespace-nowrap w-28 shrink-0' : 'wrap-anywhere') }}" data-cell="{{ key }}">{{ cells.cell(c) }}</span>{% endif %}
        {% endfor %}
        {% if actions is not empty %}
          <span data-list-actions class="ml-auto flex shrink-0 items-center gap-inline">
            {%- for key, c in actions %}<span class="whitespace-nowrap" data-cell="{{ key }}">{{ cells.cell(c) }}</span>{% endfor -%}
          </span>
        {% endif %}
        {#- THE DETAIL LINE: one sentence beneath the cells, on a line of its own,
            such as why a run failed or what its claim waits for. `detail_title`
            is the full text on hover when `detail` is a shortened form. #}
        {% if item.detail %}
          <span data-list-detail class="basis-full min-w-0 wrap-anywhere text-meta {{ detail_map[item.accent]|default('text-text-light') }}"{% if item.detail_title %} title="{{ item.detail_title }}"{% endif %}>{{ item.detail }}</span>
        {% endif %}
        {%- endif %}
      </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
{% elseif empty %}
  <div{{ (attributes ?: create_attribute()).addClass(['text-body', 'text-text-faint']) }}>{{ empty }}</div>
{% endif %}
